  "body": "### Summary\n`ComposerTouchTargetTests` should really vary Dynamic Type, so that the poll ⊖ overhang branch for a glyph wider than 44 pt is tested.\n\n### Scope\n- In `App/SwiftHFRTests/Composer/ComposerTouchTargetTests.swift:33-34`, `.appTypography(...)` is applied outside `.environment(\\.dynamicTypeSize, size)`. `ScaledFont` (`TextScale.swift:73-76`) therefore never sees the test's size: the glyph is 19.67 pt for `.xSmall`, `.large`, `.xxxLarge` and `.accessibility5` alike.\n- Fix: apply the environment outside `appTypography`, then assert that the accessibility5 glyph exceeds 44 pt (overhang 0) and that the layout still equals the glyph.\n- Also drop or reword the tautological `g + 2·overhang(g) ≥ 44` assertion (`:69-70`).\n\n### Blocked by\n#1292\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The five cases measure five different glyph sizes, and the accessibility5 case runs the overhang-0 branch.\n\nFound by the adversarial review of #1292 (Opus 5.5, r1292, round 3).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
